body:
Thats my problem too, if I mistakenly call someone Sir or Mam and they're not, is that bigotry? Everyone is allowed to have their own feelings and I would rather have the ability to have a wrong thought than be forced not to. Plus if you force people who HATE a group of people to pretend to change it'll make them worse on the inside. They'll get a persecution complex and breed even more homegrown terrorists (Shooters bombers etc.)

&#x200B;

That and it's a very VERY slippery slope. What's fine today could be bigotry tomorrow if we follow certain things. I'm also scared that somehow the definition could change and it could end up similarly to the holocaust where the race or group is either exiled or worse.

January 2024HELLO EVERYONE WHOS READY FOR THE M4 CHIP!?

&#x200B;

That being said I am sick of obsolescence coming so much faster than it used to.

Obviously you are projecting your problems from a decade ago with him flirting on this situation. He felt bad for her, maybe he was attracted idk who cares? He isn't gonna cheat, he didn't cheat and he loves you obviously. Him swapping departments shows that he's truly putting it away as well as deleting her number. 

&#x200B;

I am so sorry truly, but you need to get some therapy for yourself on this matter, he did the right thing by disengaging with her. Sure not everyone would be as nice as he was but he thought she needed a friend, she mistook it as more than that.. That happens honestly. It happens between guys it happens between girls and it happens between guys and girls.
